content.text:
Diagnosis: In parser.py, `_rest_of_line = r"[^
]*(?:|
|
)?"` tries `` before `
`, so error recovery consumes only the `` of a CRLF, leaving `
` to be absorbed as leading whitespace by the next binding. Result: invalid binding's original.string ends with bare ``, and the valid binding's original.string becomes `"
GOOD=ok
"` instead of `"GOOD=ok
"`.

Plan: Reorder the alternation to `r"[^
]*(?:
||
)?"` so CRLF is consumed as one newline. LF and lone-CR behavior stay identical, and repeated invalid lines each consume their own terminator. Single-line change in src/dotenv/parser.py; no other files.
